# The dead man's handle. Read by scripts/gen_launchd.py, which writes the plist.
# Do not hand edit the plist, edit this and generate again.
#
# This was config/launchd/templates/deadman.plist.tmpl until 2026-09-07, a whole
# hand written plist with {ROOT} through it and its 395 wake ups spelled out one
# at a time. Mo approved the kill switch and unattended operation on 2026-09-06
# and the hub ruled on 2026-09-07 that it should be armed, so the three steps
# that file listed were carried out and the file itself deleted.

[job]
name = deadman
exit_timeout = 120
run_at_load = false

[program]
{VENV_PYTHON}
{ROOT}/agent/deadman.py
--really

[environment]
TZ = America/New_York
PATH = /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin
AGENTIC_TRADING_ROOT = {ROOT}

[schedule]
# The trading day only. Outside these hours a quarter of an hour of silence is
# not a fault, it is a Tuesday evening, and the script would refuse to act
# anyway because its second question is whether the market is open.
every 5 minutes from 09:30 to 16:00 on weekdays

[comment]
The dead man's handle, run by launchd. 395 wake ups a week: 79 a day, 09:30 to
16:00 every five minutes, Monday to Friday.

WHAT IT DOES. It runs {ROOT}/agent/deadman.py in its armed form. That asks three
questions and stops at the first no: has the trading loop's heartbeat gone stale
by more than fifteen minutes, is the market actually open, and does any book
still hold a position or have an order working. If all three are yes it messages
Mo and pulls the kill switch. If any one is no it does nothing, and in the
healthy case it does not even speak to IB Gateway.

Every tick writes {ROOT}/output/heartbeat, and this job is the only thing that
reads it on a schedule. While it was unloaded that heartbeat had no reader, so a
loop that died holding a position stayed dead and holding it.

IT CAN TRADE. This is the only launchd job in the project that can. It cannot
open anything: the only orders it can cause are closing orders from
agent/kill_switch.py, and only on an account whose id starts with DU. A live
account would need AGENTIC_TRADING_KILL_LIVE set to yes in the environment block
above, which is deliberately not there and must stay that way.

Take the third argument out of the program block above and it becomes a
rehearsal: it still decides and still writes to the log, and it sends nothing
and trades nothing.

It fires once per silence, not once per wake up.
{ROOT}/output/deadman_state.json remembers which silence it already acted on,
keyed on the stale heartbeat, so a loop that stays dead all afternoon gets one
kill switch rather than seventy eight.

ARMED ON 2026-09-07 by the hub's ruling, on Mo's approval of 2026-09-06. It ran
as a dry run by hand first and reported the loop quiet with the market shut,
which is the correct answer outside trading hours.

Worth knowing: it does not fire the moment it is loaded, on purpose. A job that
fired at load would judge a heartbeat from whenever the machine was last used,
and at nine in the evening that is not a fault.
